    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d445">

                <pb facs="0486" n="452" sameAs="frus:frus1897/pg452"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Uhl to Mr.
                            Olney.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Embassy of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1897-01-13"><hi rendition="#italic">January 13, 1897</hi></date>.
                        (Received Feb. 1.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 239.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your instruction No. 256, of the 22d ultimo, in regard to the release by
                    order of the German consul at Apia, Samoa, of two sailors from the German war
                    ship <hi rendition="#italic">Falke</hi>, who had been arrested by the police at
                    Matafele, on a charge of having been drunk and disorderly and of willfully
                    damaging private property, and to inclose a copy of a note addressed by me to
                    the German foreign office, making representations on the subject as
                    directed.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Edwin F. Uhl.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d445-a1.xml" xpointer="d445-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
